# The stall we are measuring only happens when a prefault worker is parked in
# a real disk read while holding its dbreg pin, so the replicant's cache has to
# be far smaller than the working set.
#
# cachekbmin must come down too: comdb2 clamps cachekb up to cacheszkbmin
# (default 65536) as the very last sizing step, so setting cachekb alone is
# silently ignored.
cachekbmin 2048
cachekb 16384
